<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry II, Duke of Austria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1107–<a href="/years/1177">1177</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Henry II Jasomirgott, Henry Jasomirgott</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry II Jasomirgott, of the Babenberg family, was Margrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> from 1141 and also Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>. In 1156 he gave up Bavaria to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a>, and in return <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> raised Austria to a duchy by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/privilegium-minus">Privilegium Minus</a>, with special inheritance rights. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> his residence and the capital of the duchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-ii-duke-of-austria.jpg" alt="Henry II, Duke of Austria" width="320" height="339" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karl von Sava · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jas1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
